      "value": "@{5a3ad8ac4a8da67427803715|full_name}: OK so I said I'd post in the canny if I sussed anything out. I'll try to be as descriptive as I can but I think I figured something out. This issue appears to _maybe_ only affect Vive Wand users? I at least asked other users (index and oculus controllers at least) seem to be unaffected by this but then other people say they're having issues too.. Not sure on that. \nSo before the patch the way you'd move around with free movement on Vive wands was you'd press the track pad down kind of like a circular D-Pad, holding it in the direction you want to go. Let go, you'd stop moving. Used to work like free turning currently does. \nIt seems like this functionality changed post patch - now to move somewhat like before you have to press then continue keeping contact with the trackpad _without_ pressing it down. So press down, half-release to keep contact with the pad and you'll be able to move around sort of normally. \nIf you hold the button like before, it almost feels like its constantly starting and cancelling motion, creating a strange, sticky and somewhat unpredictable movement pattern. It also changes how positional adjustment feels, as its easy to accidentally keep contact on the trackpad after you think you've released. As such. you end up moving an unintuitive distance if you're trying to slightly adjust your position like you did pre-patch.\nI have no way of knowing if this change was intentional or not, but if it was I agree with OP that it probably wants to be optional. If it's not deliberate I'll try to capture some video footage of what it looks like when you hold the trackpad vs hold then keep contact without holding.\ne: Er... sorry this wasn't meant to be a reply.\ne2: I also just noticed that forward seems to be double-bound to toggle mute on/off which seems new? - Scratch that I was a dummy and accidentally unchecked the \"Disable Mic Button\" option.\ne3: Uhhh ok I just managed to fix it by checking then unchecking Vive Advanced Controls. I also just noticed I can't jump anymore. Could this be a config/binding reset issue?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
